# The fusions that owe an exact composed remainder, against the ones that do not. One row: whether
# every fusion either owes its remainder or is suspended, counted row for row, and whether no more
# fusions owe a remainder than have their demand answered.
#
# The same law on a second population
#   It is composition/owed_equality.sqlc's law on a second population. That one divides each
#   quantity's sum by that quantity's suspensions; a remainder needs both the demand and the
#   nameplate answered, so the two populations differ and each needs its own count.
#
# The `IS NULL` branch is not decoration
#   A suspension of the whole list carries no quantity at all, so a membership test written with
#   `IN` alone would quietly miss the suspension that is broader than either named one. The left
#   side would then come out larger than composition/owed_equality's.
#
# What the law also holds
#   A condition needing both quantities answered cannot cover more fusions than one needing the
#   demand alone, so the fusions owing a remainder are never more than those whose demand is
#   answered, and a breach of that is a dropped suspension rather than a disagreement about the
#   corpus. A demand is answered where its sum is owed, or where it is filed `derived` and read at
#   the figure its fusion computes; composition/owed_equality.sqlc leaves the second out, so the
#   two counts never overlap and add. The law holds it on every run.
-- composition/fusions.sqlc split by composition/suspended_remainders.sqlc, bounded by
-- composition/owed_equality.sqlc and composition/derived_fusions.sqlc on the demand.
SELECT a.slug AS law, p.subject, p.holds, p.detail
FROM      (
    :compose(algebra/roster.sqlc)
) a
LEFT JOIN (
    SELECT 'composition/owed_remainder' AS subject,
           x.total = x.kept + x.removed AND x.kept <= x.demand_owed + x.demand_derived AS holds,
           format('%s fusions: %s owing a remainder, %s suspended; '
                  '%s owe a demand sum and %s file it derived',
                  x.total, x.kept, x.removed, x.demand_owed, x.demand_derived) AS detail
    FROM ( SELECT
             (SELECT count(*) FROM ( :compose(composition/fusions.sqlc) ) f)        AS total,
             (SELECT count(*) FROM ( :compose(composition/owed_remainder.sqlc) ) o) AS kept,
             (SELECT count(*) FROM ( :compose(composition/fusions.sqlc) ) f
               WHERE EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM ( :compose(composition/suspended_remainders.sqlc) ) s
                              WHERE s.composition = f.filing AND s.composed_layer = f.layer)) AS removed,
             (SELECT count(*) FROM ( :compose(composition/owed_equality.sqlc) ) o
               WHERE o.quantity = 'demand')                                          AS demand_owed,
             (SELECT count(*) FROM ( :compose(composition/derived_fusions.sqlc) ) d
               WHERE d.quantity = 'demand')                                          AS demand_derived
         ) x
) p ON true
WHERE a.slug = 'owed_remainder'
